PN,38702
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F387A1785062907
OL,3,CMan jailed for five years over #2.4m
OL,4,Ccompany fraud
OL,6,FThames Valley Police found that
OL,7,FO'Brien fraudulently received
OL,8,F#2,418,550.91 from the company bank
OL,9,Faccount, with a further benefit of
OL,10,F#235,757.90 from unauthorised
OL,11,Ffraudulent expenses.
OL,13,FO'Brien became a financial director at
OL,14,FLiving Optics in March 2022. In
OL,15,FOctober that year he took on all
OL,16,Fresponsibilities for making payments
OL,17,Ffrom the bank.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G2/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,388,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38703
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F387A1785062907
OL,3,CMan jailed for five years over #2.4m
OL,4,Ccompany fraud
OL,6,FAfter concerns were raised he was
OL,7,Fsuspended and the company hired a
OL,8,Fforensic accountant. The investigation
OL,9,Fshowcased the widespread
OL,10,Fmisappropriation of funds by O'Brien,
OL,11,Frelating to payments that he had made
OL,12,Fto himself from the company bank
OL,13,Faccount and substantial purchases
OL,14,Fusing the company expenses system.
OL,16,FIt was also revealed he had entered
OL,17,Ftransactional data in the accounting
OL,18,Fsystem that was falsely inputted to
OL,19,Fconceal his offending.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G3/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,388,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38704
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F387A1785062907
OL,3,CMan jailed for five years over #2.4m
OL,4,Ccompany fraud
OL,6,FInvestigation officer Detective
OL,7,FConstable Pip Hankiewicz of the
OL,8,FEconomic Crime Unit said: "O'Brien
OL,9,Fabused his position of trust within
OL,10,Fthe company as well as the kindness of
OL,11,Fhis employers and colleagues at Living
OL,12,FOptics to make a gain for himself.
OL,14,F"I am glad to see the sentence given
OL,15,Fand would especially like to thank
OL,16,FLiving Optics Ltd for their time and
OL,17,Fpatience throughout this
OL,18,Finvestigation."
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G4/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,388,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38705
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F387A1785062907
OL,3,CMan jailed for five years over #2.4m
OL,4,Ccompany fraud
OL,6,FDetective Inspector Rob Havelock, Head
OL,7,Fof the Economic Crime Unit, said: "I
OL,8,Fam pleased to see the successful
OL,9,Foutcome and sentence passed on O'Brien.
OL,11,F"The defendant abused the position of
OL,12,Ftrust placed in him by his employer,
OL,13,Facting dishonestly for personal
OL,14,Ffinancial gain.
OL,16,F"His actions were deliberate and
OL,17,Fresulted in a significant financial
OL,18,Floss to the business, as well as a
OL,19,Fbreach of the trust placed in him.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G5/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
